# Migration files must keep LF line endings in the working tree.
#
# drizzle records an applied migration by the SHA-256 of the file's raw bytes,
# so a checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF (the default under
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows) changes every hash and makes `db:migrate`
# treat already-applied migrations as pending. Re-running them fails on the
# first `CREATE TABLE`/`CREATE POLICY` that already exists.
*.sql text eol=lf
